<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Enter</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>enter &lt;thing&gt;
enter &lt;door&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>enter canoe
enter portal
</pre>
<p>Climbs into something you can enter: a boat, a wagon, a portal, a tent. 
Some exits of a room are also named by a word rather than a direction, 
such as a portal or a hole; enter that word, and you go through as if you 
walked. To get out again, see <a cmd='#'>Help Leave</a>.
</p><p>You must be standing, and not fighting. Something closed must be opened 
first, and there must be room for you inside: you and what you carry must 
fit. If you are in a boat, leave it before you enter something else.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Leave</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Movement</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Sail</a>
</pre>




</div>